meta {
  name: Get Order
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

docs {
  Fetch one order fully composed: patient ref, active `items` (with their resolved
  test/panel and the per-line `discount`), the `diagnostics`/`opd`/`radiology`
  sections with resolved refs, and the active `payments` ledger. Also returns
  `orderTime` and the `billingDetails` sub-form. 404 `ORDER_NOT_FOUND` if missing,
  soft-deleted, or owned by another tenant.

  Each item's `unitPrice` is the per-line price snapshotted at order or quotation
  time (from the pricing list's `listPrice` for a catalogue line, or the
  client-supplied amount for a `direct` line — see "Create Order"). The nested
  `branchLabTest.listPrice`/`branchLabPanel.listPrice` is the catalogue line's
  **current** sellable list price (minor units) for the resolved list — the same
  value the picker/options API and `/pricing/calculate` use. An editable form
  (e.g. Update Order) should render/re-price catalogue lines from the current
  `listPrice` so the per-line price matches the server-recomputed Total/Payable;
  `unitPrice` is the historical snapshot and can differ if the list was
  re-priced. The nested `branchLabTest.priceMsrp`/`branchLabPanel.priceMsrp` is a
  **different** field again — the referenced catalogue's current master reference
  price, which is independently editable in Master Data. Do not use `priceMsrp`
  for line pricing/totals.

  Also returns the authoritative billing rollups `grossAmount`, `discountAmount`,
  `netAmount` and `paidAmount` (minor units) — the SAME derivation the Billings
  list uses (`computeBillingTotals`): a PERCENT order-discount is recomputed
  against the current item total, so these stay correct after tests are
  added/removed and never go stale relative to the items. Consumers (e.g. the
  Order Overview) should read these rather than summing the raw `payments` ledger.
  These fields are present on the get-one, create, update and cancel responses
  (all funnel through the same composer).

  Also returns `hasInvoice` (boolean) and `invoiceCode` (the linked invoice's
  number, or null): true when an invoice has been generated for this order (an
  active `InvoiceSourceOrder` link exists). An invoiced order is locked — it can
  no longer be updated (`PATCH /orders/:id`) or cancelled (`PATCH
  /orders/:id/cancel`); both return 409 `ORDER_ALREADY_INVOICED`. Cancelling the
  invoice unlinks it and returns `hasInvoice` to false.
}
